{
  "schema": "barkpark.pds.pre-gate-papers/1",
  "title": "Pre-gate published Papers \u2014 the grandfather register",
  "what_this_is": "The NAMED set of already-published Barkpark Papers whose stored blocks the Paper publish gate (Barkpark.Content.Lifecycle.prepare_paper_render_shapes/2) would refuse today. The gate runs at the publish DOOR only; nothing re-gates a published row, so these predate the gate and keep serving. The 2026-09-02 ruling GRANDFATHERS them: they stay readable and are never retroactively refused; the next EDIT of each must satisfy the gate; each carries a visible \"pre-gate\" badge until then.",
  "ruling": {
    "date": "2026-09-02",
    "verdict": "grandfather",
    "recorded_by": "lead-pds worker pds-w19, task-597ea451072da061",
    "binds": "new publishes and EDITS",
    "does_not_bind": "reads of already-published Papers \u2014 never a retroactive refusal",
    "backfill_policy": "Backfill only where a purely mechanical fix exists; otherwise the next EDIT must satisfy the gate and the Paper carries a pre-gate badge until then.",
    "ratchet": "scripts/pds-pre-gate-papers-check.sh recounts the live corpus and REFUSES if any refused published Paper is not named here. The set may SHRINK without a new ruling; it may not GROW.",
    "edit_time_mechanism": "api/test/barkpark/content/pds_w49_pre_gate_edit_rule_test.exs pins that publishing an edit of a Paper stored in either grandfathered shape is REFUSED, so \"the next edit must satisfy the gate\" is a mechanism and not prose."
  },
