      "refusal_message": "blocks[N].head.cells[M] has no renderable inline content",
      "offending_cell": "table block `header` (legacy spelling of `head`) whose cells are bare strings",
      "reader_behaviour": "GRANDFATHERED. The reader renders this shape CORRECTLY \u2014 proven by composing the live block through Render.Compose.compose_block/2: the header text reaches the page as <th ...><span>Moment</span></th>. The refusal is a NORMALISER/VALIDATOR key asymmetry, not reader debt: BlockOps.validate_render_shapes/1 reads `Map.get(block, \"head\") || Map.get(block, \"header\")`, while BlockOps.normalize_table_leaves/1 rescues bare-string cells under `\"head\"` ONLY. So the legacy `\"header\"` spelling is validated but never normalised. Nothing is lost to a reader today; the cost of the ruling is that the next EDIT of any of these 37 Papers is refused on a header that renders perfectly.",
      "reader_impact": "none",
      "ruling": "grandfathered",
      "mechanical_fix": {
        "exists": true,
        "kind": "normaliser, not per-paper backfill",
        "where": "api/lib/barkpark/content/papers/block_ops.ex \u2014 normalize_table_leaves/1",
        "patch": "normalise the legacy \"header\" spelling the validator already reads, exactly as \"head\" is normalised",
        "applied": false,
        "why_not_applied": "It changes GATE behaviour for every future publish, which is a new ruling, not the execution of this one. It is also outside this row's fence (api/lib) and this row's criteria are met without it. Filed as follow-up work; see PR body."
