      "refusal_reason": "table_cell_no_inline_content",
      "refusal_message": "blocks[N].head.cells[M] has no renderable inline content",
      "offending_cell": "table block `head` holding a list of ROW objects instead of a list of cells",
      "reader_behaviour": "GRANDFATHERED, WITH REAL READER LOSS. `head` holds a LIST containing a ROW object (`[%{\"cells\" => [cell, cell]}]`) instead of the cells themselves. Render.Compose table_row_cells/1 List.wraps the outer list, so the ROW OBJECT becomes the single cell; table_cell_content/1 falls to its catch-all and returns the map; Inline.compose_inline_children/1 has no map clause and returns []. The page answers 200 and renders ONE EMPTY <th> where two labels \u2014 \"Corner\" and \"Verdict\" \u2014 were authored. This is the only Paper of the 38 whose readers actually lose content.",
      "reader_impact": "blank_header_cell",
      "ruling": "grandfathered",
      "mechanical_fix": {
        "exists": true,
        "kind": "per-paper backfill, derivable",
        "where": "the stored Paper studio-space-priority-desk-advance-2026-07-19, block dg-cov-t",
        "patch": "unwrap TWICE, to the CELLS: head: [%{\"cells\" => cs}] -> head: cs. The obvious one-level unwrap (head: %{\"cells\" => cs}) is a TRAP: the gate ACCEPTS it (validate_render_shapes/1 routes a %{\"cells\" => list} head through render_table_row_errors/2 and finds every cell renderable) but Render.Compose only promotes head to a header row when is_list(declared_head), so a MAP head renders NO <thead> at all. Gate-green, header still gone. Pinned by pds_w49_pre_gate_edit_rule_test.exs \"the OBVIOUS repair ... satisfies the gate and STILL loses the header\".",
        "applied": false,
        "why_not_applied": "A live write to a published Paper on the prod ledger. This worker was fenced to tooling/pds, scripts/pds-* and one test file and told not to rewrite any paper. This is the ONE row where the ruling's backfill clause bites; it is handed to the lead named, with the exact derivable patch, rather than executed unauthorised."
      },
